"A phone has no room for a fan, so it spreads the heat through its body and lets it leave from the surface. That is why you feel the warmth in your hand. If a chip still gets too hot, it protects itself: it slows down so that it makes less heat. You may notice a game becoming less smooth. If slowing down is not enough, the device shuts itself off.": "bdd9c6cd7039",
"Engineers work hard to make chips that waste less energy. The best trick is lowering the voltage, because a small drop in voltage saves a lot of power. Chips also rest whenever they can, which makes a battery last longer. For the biggest computers, air is not enough, and some are cooled with liquid instead. A cooler chip is a faster and longer-lasting chip.": "a506aa6bf894",
