"Play a game on a phone for a while, and the back of the phone grows warm. Open many programs on a laptop, and a fan inside begins to spin loudly. Nothing is burning, and nothing is broken. The heat comes from the chip, and making heat is a normal part of a chip's work.": "7b593c9d2e58",
"Play a game on a phone for a while, and the back of the phone grows warm. Open many programs on a laptop, and a fan inside begins to spin loudly. Nothing is burning, and nothing is broken. The heat comes from the chip, and making heat is a normal part of a chip's work. Remember that a chip is made of transistors, which are tiny switches. Each time a switch turns on or off, a little electric charge has to move, and moving it takes a little energy. That energy does not disappear. It turns into heat. One switch makes almost no heat at all, but a chip has billions of switches, and they can switch billions of times every second. So the harder a chip works, the hotter it gets. When your phone is only showing the clock, few transistors are switching, and the chip stays cool. When you play a game, the chip must draw a new picture many times a second. Many more transistors switch, the chip uses more power, and it makes more heat. The heat has to go somewhere. In a computer, a piece of metal called a heat sink sits on top of the chip. It has many thin fins, so it has a very large surface that touches the air. Heat moves from the chip into the metal and from the metal into the air. A fan then blows the warm air away so that cooler air can take its place. A phone has no room for a fan, so it spreads the heat through its body and lets it leave from the surface. That is why you feel the warmth in your hand. If a chip still gets too hot, it protects itself: it slows down so that it makes less heat. You may notice a game becoming less smooth. If slowing down is not enough, the device shuts itself off. Engineers work hard to make chips that waste less energy. The best trick is lowering the voltage, because a small drop in voltage saves a lot of power. Chips also rest whenever they can, which makes a battery last longer. For the biggest computers, air is not enough, and some are cooled with liquid instead. A cooler chip is a faster and longer-lasting chip.": "691c87c26137",
